<title>FRANCE: Snapshot of world defence industry.</title>
<headline>Snapshot of world defence industry.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel Alsthom SA and Dassault Industries on Tuesday gave the following snapshot of the world defence industry during a news conference on their joint bid for the state's 58-percent stake in Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>(In billions of francs)</p>
<p>Name				Sales    Defence sales    Market</p>
<p>								     capitalisation (May 5)</p>
<p>Lockheed Martin</p>
<p>Loral (LML)			 190	 90		  120</p>
<p>Boeing /MDD			 210	 30		  350</p>
<p>Raytheon Hughes		   120	 70		   60</p>
<p>GEC				    86	 26		   90</p>
<p>British Aerospace		  60	 10		   50</p>
<p>Daimler-Benz			350	 15		  230</p>
<p>Thomson-CSF			  36	 23		   22</p>
<p>Aerospatiale /</p>
<p>Dassault			     60	  9		30/35</p>
<p>Alcatel Alsthom		   160	  8.6		103</p>
<p>Lagardere Groupe		   50	  8		   18</p>
<p>Dassault Elec.			4.5	3		    3</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
